# AXIS SIBLING (Track L) — resource-carrying inner-element cell (String) of
# `guard_tuple_field_writethrough.gg`. Element type = String exercises the
# resource-typed tuple element path — the fix must not introduce a double-free
# or leak when the write REPLACES an owned resource in the guarded tuple.
# Pre-fix RED: C compile-fail (same `no member 'owner'`), LLVM builds but prints
# garbage. Post-fix: `world\n1` — the previous "hello" is dropped by the tuple's
# in-place field-store; the new String is owned by the guarded tuple.
#
# ASan / leak-freedom coverage: this fixture also exercises the resource-typed
# tuple-element WRITE ownership handoff; if the fix leaks or double-frees, the
# `security` ASan sweep will catch it (parent's round-close gate).
void main():
    Mutex[(String, int)] m = Mutex[(String, int)](("hello", 1))
    Guard[(String, int)] g = m.lock()
    g.0 = "world"
    print(g.0)
    print(g.1)
